
  Every record is the same object in both runtimes:

  { [36mts[39m: [31m"2026-09-16T14:03:11.204Z"[39m, [36mlevel[39m: [31m"warn"[39m, [36mname[39m: [31m"auth"[39m, [36mmsg[39m: [31m"login rejected"[39m, [36mctx[39m: {...} }

  [38;5;153mts[39m as an ISO string rather than epoch millis — these logs are read by a human out of a file or a devtools dump, not by
  a parser, and readability wins. This is the one part of the design that's expensive to change later, since anything
  that ever reads a persisted log depends on it.

  [1mRedaction mechanics.[0m [38;5;153mredact.js[39m exports a single [38;5;153mPERMITTED[39m set of key names and a [38;5;153mredact(ctx)[39m function. Anything not in
  the set is replaced by the string [38;5;153m"[redacted]"[39m rather than dropped — if a field was present and got scrubbed, you
  want to see that it existed, otherwise you spend debugging time wondering whether the code path ran at all. The key
  name is revealed; the value never is.

  It recurses to every depth, so a permitted key holding a nested object doesn't become a hole in the policy, with a
  depth cap and a total-size cap so one bad call site can't fill the ring buffer with a single record. [38;5;153mError[39m values are
  special-cased to [38;5;153m{ name, message, stack }[39m — a logging layer that swallows stack traces isn't worth having.

  [1mThe honest limitation.[0m The allow-list governs [38;5;153mctx[39m only. Nothing stops someone writing [38;5;153mlog.info("password is " + [39m
  [38;5;153mpassword)[39m, and no redactor can catch that, because by then it's an opaque string. The mitigation is convention — [38;5;153mmsg[39m
  is a static description, all variable data goes in [38;5;153mctx[39m — plus review. I'd rather state that plainly than imply the
  allow-list makes the logger leak-proof.

  [1mInitial permitted set.[0m [38;5;153musername[39m, [38;5;153muserId[39m, [38;5;153mevent[39m, [38;5;153mdurationMs[39m, [38;5;153mstatus[39m, [38;5;153merrorCode[39m, [38;5;153mformField[39m. That's what the current code
  would actually need. [38;5;153musername[39m deserves a deliberate decision rather than a default, which is the question below.
